    shared-term floor (all route-unique terms -> 0) with S_gas x0.25 and S_HF x0.25 (ladder-quality distances for the Hubble-flow routes): 0.0167 dex
    shared-term floor (all route-unique terms -> 0) with S_gas, S_star and S_HF all x0.25: 0.0096 dex
  ALMA 2026-11-06 / 11-28: required M_gas ~ 1/a0 (lever -1), so the whole kappa interval is +-0.098 dex in required gas; the stellar-mass branch moves it 0.6 dex, the KURVS floor is 0.15 dex, F-DESI vs F-flat differ <= 0.02 dex. Best reachable a0 precision >= 0.15 dex > 0.049 dex: cannot pin kappa. The tests decide the z-dependence (flat vs dark-energy-tracking vs H(z)), not the level.
  Gaia DR4 2026-12-02: current canonical prediction is Newtonian (gamma_v - 1 <= 8.9e-4 at 50 kAU), lever on kappa = 0. Under the superseded MI prescription (22% of a0 -> 3.3% of gamma_v, lever 0.382 per dex) the frozen sigma_sys 0.02 gives 0.052 dex > 0.049: cannot pin kappa either, and it constrains the prescription, not a0.
